# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the $4 \\times 4$ lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"
msgstr "Simule a rede $4 \\times 4$ {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the $4 \\times 4$ lattice, you can do both: compute the exact state at every coupling, and sample every circuit with 10,000 shots, as an experiment would. The shots are stored with shape (batches, shots, qubits), the same layout as the randomizations in the hardware data. Here all 10,000 shots form a single batch, so the bootstrap over batches adds no shot noise, and the error bars in the next plot show only the spread between marginal positions.\n"
msgstr "Para a rede $4 \\times 4$, você pode fazer as duas coisas: calcular o estado exato em cada acoplamento e amostrar cada circuito com 10.000 shots, como um experimento faria. Os shots são armazenados com o formato (lotes, shots, qubits), o mesmo layout das randomizações nos dados de hardware. Aqui, todos os 10.000 shots formam um único lote, então o bootstrap sobre os lotes não adiciona ruído de shots, e as barras de erro no próximo gráfico mostram apenas a dispersão entre as posições das marginais.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. What to measure and how to estimate it {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"
msgstr "2. O que medir e como estimá-lo {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR and the collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"
msgstr "O IPR e a entropia de colisão {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a marginal $A$ of $n_A$ qubits with bitstring distribution $p_A(a)$, the quantity to estimate is the inverse participation ratio (IPR) of the marginal distribution, and from it the collision entropy:\n"
msgstr "Para uma marginal $A$ de $n_A$ qubits com distribuição de bitstrings $p_A(a)$, a quantidade a estimar é a razão de participação inversa (IPR) da distribuição marginal e, a partir dela, a entropia de colisão:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is also the probability that two shots agree on the marginal. A product state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, and a random state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, so $S_2$ climbs from 0 to about $n_A$ bits as the marginal becomes random.\n"
msgstr "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ também é a probabilidade de que dois shots coincidam na marginal. Um estado produto tem $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, e um estado aleatório tem $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, então $S_2$ sobe de 0 a cerca de $n_A$ bits à medida que a marginal se torna aleatória.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 1: count pairs of shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"
msgstr "Estimador 1: contar pares de shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How do you estimate this quantity from your shots?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Como você estima essa quantidade a partir dos seus shots?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The naive estimator computes each $p(a)$ from the shots as $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, then sums $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"This estimator is biased.\n"
msgstr ""
"O estimador ingênuo calcula cada $p(a)$ a partir dos shots como $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$ e depois soma $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"Esse estimador é enviesado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ counts every shot as agreeing with itself, which pushes the estimate up: on average it gives $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ instead of $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Since $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is the probability that two shots agree, count only pairs of *different* shots:\n"
msgstr "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ conta cada shot como coincidindo consigo mesmo, o que eleva a estimativa: em média, ele dá $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ em vez de $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Como $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ é a probabilidade de que dois shots coincidam, conte apenas pares de shots *diferentes*:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is unbiased, and it is what `ipr_from_shots` below computes.\n"
msgstr "Esse estimador é não enviesado, e é isso que `ipr_from_shots` abaixo calcula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"
msgstr "Estimador 2: expansão de Parseval {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR can also be written through the parities $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ of all nonempty subsets $S$ of the marginal:\n"
msgstr "O IPR também pode ser escrito por meio das paridades $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ de todos os subconjuntos não vazios $S$ da marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This form matters because error mitigation methods such as PEA work on expectation values, not on probabilities.\n"
"**One qubit:** The outcome probabilities are $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ and $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, so\n"
msgstr ""
"Essa forma é importante porque métodos de mitigação de erros como o PEA trabalham com valores esperados, não com probabilidades.\n"
"**Um qubit:** As probabilidades dos resultados são $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ e $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, portanto\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**A $2 \\times 2$ marginal:** With its qubits labeled $a, b, c, d$, the marginal has $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parities: 4 single qubits, 6 pairs, 4 triples, and the whole marginal, so\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**Uma marginal $2 \\times 2$:** Com seus qubits rotulados como $a, b, c, d$, a marginal tem $2^4 - 1 = 15$ paridades: 4 qubits individuais, 6 pares, 4 trios e a marginal inteira, portanto\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

